      "writingTasks": [
        {
          "task": "Paraphrasing Guidelines & Key Principles",
          "content": "What is Paraphrasing?\nParaphrasing is re-writing the poet's words or ideas in your own clear prose without altering the fundamental meaning. A stanza takes the shape of natural prose sentences. It is about the same length as the original, because the purpose is to re-phrase without omitting any important thoughts.\n\nEssential Rules for Paraphrasing a Poem:\n1. Mark thought groups and understand the complete sentence structure across line breaks.\n2. Replace inverted poetic syntax with standard Subject + Verb + Object word order.\n3. Replace archaic or poetic vocabulary with simple, everyday words.\n4. Maintain the original grammatical voice and perspective (first person if the poet speaks directly)."
        },
        {
          "task": "A. Paraphrase of Second Stanza (Textbook Assignment)",
          "topicSentence": "Continuous as the stars that shine / And twinkle on the Milky Way...",
          "content": "Model Paraphrase:\nThe poet explains that the golden daffodils grew in an unbroken, continuous line along the shore of the bay, resembling the countless shining stars that twinkle across the Milky Way. In a single instantaneous glance, the poet saw thousands of blooming daffodils actively moving and nodding their heads in a lively, energetic dance."
        },
        {
          "task": "Complete Solved Paraphrases for All Stanzas (Reference Suite)",
          "content": "• Stanza 1 Paraphrase:\nThe poet says that one day he was strolling alone and aimlessly across the hills and valleys, just like a solitary cloud drifting high in the sky. Suddenly, he came across a vast multitude of bright golden daffodils growing beside the lake under the trees, fluttering and swaying gracefully in the gentle breeze.\n\n• Stanza 2 Paraphrase:\nThe poet notes that the flowers stretched in an endless line along the lake's margin, just like the innumerable stars that sparkle in the Milky Way. In a single look, he saw ten thousand daffodils tossing their golden heads in a cheerful and vigorous dance.\n\n• Stanza 3 Paraphrase:\nThe poet observes that although the glittering waves of the lake were also dancing, the radiant daffodils surpassed the sparkling waters in sheer delight. A poet could not help but feel joyful in such cheerful and lively company. He continued to gaze at the scene for a long time, unaware of the immense lasting wealth and spiritual joy this sight had bestowed upon him.\n\n• Stanza 4 Paraphrase:\nThe poet reflects that whenever he rests on his couch in a vacant or thoughtful and sorrowful mood, the visual memory of those daffodils suddenly flashes upon his inner mind, which is the true blessing of solitude. Then his heart is immediately filled with happiness and begins to dance in unison with the daffodils."
        },
        {
          "task": "B. Guidelines for Summarizing a Poem & Comprehensive Summary of 'The Daffodils'",
          "content": "Rules for Summarizing a Poem:\n1. Read the poem thoroughly to grasp the central theme and development.\n2. Note down only the salient, indispensable points and discard minor descriptions.\n3. Arrange the main points in logical, chronological order.\n4. A summary should be concise, objective, written in simple prose, and roughly one-third the length of the original.\n\nSolved Comprehensive Summary of 'The Daffodils':\n'The Daffodils' by William Wordsworth is a celebrated Romantic poem that glorifies the healing, everlasting charm of nature. While wandering lonely as a cloud across hills and vales, the poet unexpectedly encounters a vast host of golden daffodils blooming along the edge of a lake beneath the trees. The flowers stretch in an endless line like twinkling stars in the Milky Way, dancing vigorously in the spring breeze. Although the sparkling lake waves dance beside them, the vibrant daffodils outshine the waters in pure joy. The poet gazes in deep fascination, receiving an invaluable spiritual treasure. Later, whenever the poet lies on his couch in a thoughtful, vacant, or sad mood, the memory of the daffodils flashes upon his 'inward eye'—the supreme blessing of solitude. His heart fills with overwhelming delight and dances joyfully alongside the daffodils."
        }
      ],
