          "explanation": "A Simile compares two unlike things using 'as' or 'like' ('lonely as a cloud'). Personification gives human attributes to non-human entities ('daffodils dancing'). Hyperbole uses deliberate exaggeration ('Ten thousand saw I at a glance'). Imagery uses sensory language appealing to sight, sound, or touch ('golden daffodils', 'sparkling waves').",
