          "answer": "In an era dominated by concrete jungles, digital screens, and high-stress urban routines, humanity is suffering from profound ecological alienation and spiritual fatigue.\n\n1. The Healing Psychology of Nature:\nModern psychological research corroborates what Romantic poets like Wordsworth intuited centuries ago: immersion in natural green spaces significantly reduces cortisol (stress hormone) levels, lowers blood pressure, enhances creative cognition, and relieves chronic anxiety. Natural beauty stimulates the release of endorphins and fosters mindful tranquility.\n\n2. Spiritual Transcendence in Nature:\nBoth Eastern and Western philosophies revere nature as a sacred mirror of divine artistry. Allama Iqbal viewed nature as a dynamic canvas inspiring youth toward soaring ambition, while Wordsworth regarded it as a moral guide and nurse of the human soul. When humans witness mountains, flowing rivers, and blooming flora, they recognize their humble place in the cosmic order.\n\nConclusion:\nPreserving natural parks and regularly communing with the outdoors is not a luxury; it is vital medicine for the human body, mind, and soul."
