    "englishTranslation": "Complete Lesson: The Madina Charter represents the dawn of constitutional democracy, human rights, religious pluralism, and collective security, established by Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) in 622 CE.",
    "englishSummary": "Unit 5 details the historical significance of the Madina Charter (Mithaq-e-Madina), drafted in 622 CE by Hazrat Muhammad (PBUH). Faced with a fractured society composed of Muslim immigrants, native Ansar, Jewish tribes, and polytheists, the Prophet created the world's first written constitution. It established a multi-faith confederation, guaranteed religious liberty, instituted judicial equality, abolished tribal vendettas, and mandated mutual defense against external aggression. The Charter anticipated modern constitutional principles and the UN Declaration of Human Rights by fourteen centuries.",
