      "grammar": [
        {
          "topic": "Conditional Sentences: Zero, First, Second, and Third Conditionals",
          "explanation": "Conditionals express relationships between conditions and results:\n- Zero Conditional (Universal facts): If + Present Simple, Present Simple ('If you heat water, it boils').\n- First Conditional (Real future possibility): If + Present Simple, Will + base verb ('If we study digitally, we will excel').\n- Second Conditional (Hypothetical present/future): If + Past Simple, Would + base verb ('If I had a supercomputer, I would build AI models').\n- Third Conditional (Unfulfilled past): If + Past Perfect, Would have + V3 ('If they had secured data, the hack would have failed').",
          "examples": [
            "Type 1: If you update your software, your system will remain secure.",
            "Type 2: If students spent less time on social media, their grades would improve.",
            "Type 3: If he had backed up his files, he would not have lost his project."
          ]
        }
      ],
