          "question": "Q1. Define First Aid and state its three fundamental objectives.",
          "marks": "4 Marks",
          "answer": "First Aid is the immediate care and assistance administered to an injured or suddenly ill person before professional medical personnel arrive.\n\nIts three primary objectives ('The 3 Ps') are:\n1. Preserve Life: Prevent premature death through basic airway maintenance, CPR, or stopping hemorrhage.\n2. Prevent Deterioration: Keep the victim's medical condition from worsening (e.g., stabilizing fractures, cooling burns).\n3. Promote Recovery: Facilitate early healing by dressing wounds, reassuring the casualty, and easing pain."
