      "writingTasks": {
        "applicationTrip": {
          "title": "Model Application: Request for a Recreational Trip (Textbook Page 129)",
          "content": "The Principal,\nGovernment High School,\nHayatabad Peshawar.\n\nSubject: Request for a Recreational Trip\n\nSir,\nWith due respect I request you to allow our Grade 9th-A to go to Nathiagali on a recreational trip. Since exams are over, we want to enjoy and relax.\nIt is requested to kindly arrange a recreational trip for us.\nI shall be very grateful for this act of kindness.\n\nYour obedient student,\nSaad Inam\n(Monitor) 9th-A\nDate: Dec. 12, 2017"
        },
        "applicationRemissionFine": {
          "title": "Exercise A: Application to Principal for Remission of Fine",
          "content": "To,\nThe Principal,\nGovernment High School No. 1, Peshawar.\n\nSubject: Application for Remission of Absence Fine\n\nRespected Sir,\nMost respectfully, it is submitted that I could not attend school for three consecutive days (from 15th to 17th October) due to severe seasonal flu and fever. Because of my sudden illness, I was unable to submit a timely leave application. Consequently, a fine of Rs. 300 has been imposed on me.\n\nSir, my father is a low-income laborer and it is very difficult for him to pay this fine. I have always been a punctual, disciplined, and studious student with an unblemished academic record.\n\nI kindly request you to remit my absence fine on medical grounds. I shall be immensely grateful for your benevolent consideration.\n\nYours obediently,\nMuhammad Hamza\nClass: 9th-B, Roll No: 24\nDate: October 18, 2026"
        },
        "emailFriendExam": {
          "title": "Exercise B: Informal Email Congratulating Friend on Exam Success",
          "content": "From: bilal.khan@email.com\nTo: zarak.ahmed@email.com\nSubject: Heartiest Congratulations on Your Outstanding Board Exam Result!\n\nDear Zarak,\n\nI hope this email finds you in the best of health and spirits.\n\nI was absolutely thrilled to learn today that you secured 1st position in our district in the Class 9 Board Examinations, scoring 96% marks! Please accept my heartiest congratulations on this spectacular achievement.\n\nYour tireless dedication, late-night study sessions, and perseverance have truly paid off. You have made your parents, teachers, and all of us immensely proud. We must plan a celebration get-together soon.\n\nConvey my warmest regards to uncle and aunt.\n\nYour sincere friend,\nBilal Khan"
        },
        "emailEditorRoadAccidents": {
          "title": "Exercise C: Formal Email to Newspaper Editor on Road Accidents and Rash Driving",
          "content": "From: rashid.citizen@email.com\nTo: editor.dailyexpress@email.com\nSubject: Urgent Need to Curb Rash Driving and Reckless Traffic Violations in Peshawar\n\nDear Sir,\n\nThrough the esteemed columns of your widely circulated newspaper, I wish to draw the urgent attention of the City Traffic Police and municipal authorities toward the alarming surge in road accidents caused by rash driving in Peshawar.\n\nDaily commuters, especially school children and elderly pedestrians, face grave peril due to underage motorcycling, speeding dumpers, and blatant disregard for red lights on major arteries like University Road and Ring Road. The lack of strict helmet enforcement and reckless overtaking create constant hazards.\n\nI urge the traffic administration to deploy electronic speed-monitoring cameras, install prominent pedestrian zebra crossings, impound vehicles driven by unlicensed juveniles, and organize road safety awareness campaigns.\n\nThank you for your consideration.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRashid Mahmood\nResident of Hayatabad Phase 4, Peshawar"
        },
        "letterDirectorSanitary": {
          "title": "Exercise D: Formal Letter to Director PDA on Sanitary Conditions",
          "content": "House No. 42, Sector F-3,\nPhase 6, Hayatabad, Peshawar.\nOctober 20, 2026\n\nThe Director,\nPeshawar Development Authority (PDA),\nCommercial Complex, Hayatabad, Peshawar.\n\nSubject: Deteriorating Sanitary Conditions and Garbage Disposal in Phase 6\n\nRespected Sir,\nI wish to bring to your immediate notice the appalling sanitary conditions currently prevailing in Sector F-3 of Hayatabad Phase 6.\n\nFor the past three weeks, municipal garbage collection trucks have failed to visit our neighborhood regularly. As a result, huge heaps of domestic refuse have accumulated along street corners, giving off foul odors and turning into breeding grounds for mosquitoes and stray animals. The clogged open drains are overflowing with wastewater, posing severe health hazards of dengue and typhoid.\n\nI earnestly request your good office to dispatch sanitation squads for immediate garbage removal and fumigation of the locality.\n\nThanking you in anticipation.\n\nYours faithfully,\nKamran Tariq\nPresident, Residents' Welfare Association, Phase 6"
        }
      },
