          "answer": "Email communication adheres to distinct stylistic conventions based on audience and context.\n\n1. Purpose & Audience:\n- Formal Emails: Written for academic, official, or business purposes to superiors, institutions, or clients.\n- Informal Emails: Written for personal updates to friends, relatives, and peers.\n\n2. Language, Tone & Accuracy:\n- Formal: Professional, courteous, grammatically rigorous; strictly prohibits slang, emoticons, or contractions ('I will not' rather than 'I won't').\n- Informal: Warm, spontaneous, relaxed; contractions ('I'm', 'can't', 'LOL') and exclamation marks are natural.\n\n3. Structure & Sign-offs:\n- Formal: Begins with 'Dear Mr. Khan / Dear Sir' and closes with 'Yours sincerely / Kind regards'.\n- Informal: Opens with 'Hi / Hello' and closes with 'Best wishes / Love / Cheers'."
