        "essayHaqooqUlEbad": {
          "title": "Essay: Haqooq-ul-Ebad — Rights of Fellow Human Beings (100–150 Words)",
          "content": "In Islamic jurisprudence and universal ethics, human duties are broadly categorized into two spheres: 'Haqooq-Allah' (the Rights of Allah, such as prayer and fasting) and 'Haqooq-ul-Ebad' (the Rights of Fellow Human Beings). While Almighty Allah may forgive shortcomings in His personal worship out of His infinite mercy, He has ordained that violations against fellow human beings will not be forgiven until the wronged individual pardons them.\n\nHaqooq-ul-Ebad encompasses treating parents with utmost kindness, supporting orphans, aiding neighbors regardless of faith, providing charity to the poor, maintaining honesty in business, and safeguarding others from harm. Serving suffering humanity is the greatest manifestation of faith. A society grounded in Haqooq-ul-Ebad fosters universal brotherhood, social justice, and lasting peace."
        },
