          "answer": "Narration transformation requires precise adherence to syntactic and deictic shift rules.\n\n1. Assertive Statements:\n- Reporting verb in Past tense causes backshifting: Present Simple -> Past Simple ('gives' -> 'gave'), Present Perfect -> Past Perfect ('have won' -> 'had won').\n- Universal Truths remain unchanged: 'The earth moves around the sun.'\n\n2. Interrogative Sentences:\n- Converted using 'asked' or 'inquired'.\n- Auxiliary questions take 'if/whether': 'He asked me if I had brought the pens.'\n- Wh-questions retain the wh-word: 'He asked where I was going.'\n\n3. Imperatives (Requests/Commands):\n- Use infinitive 'to + base verb': 'She requested him to wait there till she returned.'\n\n4. Exclamatory Sentences:\n- Use 'exclaimed with joy/sorrow' and convert exclamations to statements: 'Alice exclaimed that she was very clever.'"
