          "answer": "Islam is a complete code of life rooted in justice, compassion, and the preservation of human dignity through 'Haqooq-ul-Ebad'.\n\n1. Theological Primacy:\nIn the Farewell Sermon (Khutbatul Wada), the Holy Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) declared the life, honor, and property of every human being to be sacred and inviolable. Allah will pardon lapses in ritual obligations, but injustice against fellow humans must be reconciled directly with the victim.\n\n2. Key Dimensions:\n- Filial Reverence: Utmost respect and support for elderly parents.\n- Care for the Vulnerable: Protecting orphans, widows, and destitute laborers.\n- Universal Neighborliness: The Prophet (PBUH) emphasized kindness to neighbors regardless of religious affiliation.\n\n3. Humanitarian Synthesis:\nAbou Ben Adhem epitomizes this Islamic ideal: true spiritual greatness is achieved not in isolated contemplation, but through active relief of human distress."
