          "answer": "Voice transformation shifts focus from the doer of the action (active) to the recipient of the action (passive).\n\n1. Transformation Rules:\n- The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive sentence.\n- Use the appropriate auxiliary form of 'be' matching the tense and number of the new subject.\n- The main verb is always converted to its Past Participle (V3) form.\n- The original subject is placed after the preposition 'by' (or omitted if generic).\n\n2. Tense Models from Unit 15:\n- Past Simple: 'The teacher praised the boy' -> 'The boy was praised by the teacher.'\n- Present Continuous: 'They are painting the walls' -> 'The walls are being painted by them.'\n- Present Perfect: 'The mechanic has fixed the car' <-> 'The car has been fixed by the mechanic.'\n- Double Object: 'She gave the beggar a five rupee coin' -> 'The beggar was given a five-rupee coin by her.'"
